# board-start -- past the board settings and into Toad's Midway Madness.
#
# The same walk as ref/movies/board-start.txt (the Dolphin side), rebased on
# where the port actually is: the console spends 186 frames on the cold-boot
# logos and 4,195 on the opening THP movie, and the port skips the movie
# outright and loads off a local disc image, so it arrives at the title around
# frame 700.
#
# The shape is what the two sides share, and nothing in it is pinned to a
# frame, because no prompt in this run is at a frame either side can predict --
# the new-file card scene's length moves everything after it:
#
#   START through the boot,
#   then A for four frames out of every sixty-four,
#   and START for four frames out of every two hundred and fifty-six,
#   thirty-two frames out of phase with the A.
#
# The second metronome is there because the minigame instruction screen ends on
# START and nothing else (src/REL/instDll/main.c:293), and the phase offset is
# there because that test is an equality against PAD_BUTTON_START: an A on the
# same frame makes it 0x1100 and it matches nothing.
#
# 1P + 3 COM on EASY is what the character-select and board-settings defaults
# give, so no stick input is needed to set that up.

# Accept the title.
at 700 6 START
at 750 6 START
at 800 6 START
at 850 6 START
at 900 6 START
at 950 6 START
at 1000 6 START
at 1050 6 START
at 1100 6 START

# A, four frames out of every sixty-four; START, four out of every 256.
at 1160 4 A
at 1192 4 START
at 1224 4 A
at 1288 4 A
at 1352 4 A
at 1416 4 A
at 1448 4 START
